    "methods_description": "EEG data were acquired at 1000 Hz using a 64-channel Neuroscan Quik-Cap with SynAmps2 amplifier, referenced to the right mastoid with forehead ground. The system recorded 66 total channels (64 EEG + 1 EOG + 1 stim). Concurrent eye-tracking and high-speed video recordings captured ocular activity during motor imagery execution. Participants performed two-class hand motor imagery tasks (left and right hand grasping) with visual rectangle cues, 40 trials per session across up to 3 sessions.",
